mynx's changes to Termux:X11 (scripts/build-x11.sh applies them). Like the
code they change, they're under the GPL-3.0 (Termux:X11's LICENSE), not
mynx's MIT licence.

- activity.cpp: only CmdEntryPoint's classes are loaded (no activity), so
  only its natives are registered.
- cmdentrypoint.cpp: the knock port (7892) listens on 127.0.0.1 only, not
  on every network.
- renderer.cpp: until a view says its size, the screen fills the surface.
- CmdEntryPoint.java: libXlorie.so is loaded from MYNX_X11_LIB (the app's
  native library dir), as it isn't inside the jar.
- The extended screen (another phone as a screen of this one): the app
  lays out the other phone's part of the screen (event 100: mode 1 a
  second RandR monitor "mynx-b" on a CRTC of its own, placed where the
  app says; mode 2 one monitor as big as both phones; 0 neither), and
  InitOutput.c sends back what each surface shows (event 101). The
  renderer draws this phone's part into the view's surface and the other
  phone's into a second surface, an encoder's
  (ICmdEntryInterface.mynxSecondWindowChanged, transaction 6), also while
  this phone's view has no surface.

